<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asan Kaigy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Asan Qaiğy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asan Kaigy was a semi-legendary poet and thinker of the fifteenth century, remembered as the first great zhyrau, or poet-adviser, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a> and an adviser to Kazakh khans. In tradition he searched the steppe on a swift <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camel</a> for Zheruiyk, a promised land of plenty where people would live without want. His verses, preserved orally, are among the earliest of Kazakh literature and shared with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nogais">Nogais</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a>.</p></div>
